{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789910182,"nonce":"vSDsdrLNgmSOmY8iopWD72y3VYg=","title":"Lua: table.concat is quadratic","message":"`zl_table_concat` folds `acc = acc .. piece .. sep` over the table, so joining n pieces copies the growing result n times: two allocations per element, each the full length so far. On the tokenize benchmark (300k parts, 2.5 MB result) that is on the order of 750 GB copied and, with the collector's large-block gap (see the collector issue), several GB resident. PUC Lua uses a buffer and joins in one pass.\n\nFix: collect the pieces into a `List\u003cString\u003e` and join once through the string plugin's `$String$join_n`, which sizes the result once and copies each piece in.","files":null}]}